        <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:eizehu_mekoman/4">
          <tei:p>4. The burnt-offering was one of the most holy sacrifices. It was slaughtered on the north side of the altar. Its blood, which was there received in a sacred vessel, required two sprinklings [at opposite angles of the altar] making four in all. This offering had to be flayed, severed into parts, and consumed by fire.</tei:p>
        </tei:div>
